## Scale Factors					
Data/MC scale factors are provided for each working point and should be applied when using simulated events. The scale factors are available in JSON format and can be accessed through the correction library.

Example Usage¶
import correctionlib
evaluator = correctionlib.CorrectionSet.from_file("electron.json")

# Get scale factor
sf = evaluator["Electron-ID-SF"].evaluate("2022Re-recoBCD", "sf", "Medium", eta, pt)
Validation and Performance¶
The cut-based electron ID has been extensively validated using:

Tag-and-probe studies with Z→ee events
Electron efficiency measurements in data and MC
Background rejection studies using QCD samples
Systematic uncertainty evaluations
Recommendations¶
Use the official VID implementation in CMSSW
Apply appropriate data/MC scale factors
Consider systematic uncertainties in your analysis
For custom selections, validation with the EGM POG is required
Configuration Example¶
# Add to your analysis configuration
process.load("RecoEgamma.ElectronIdentification.ElectronIDValueMapProducer_cfi")
process.load("RecoEgamma.ElectronIdentification.heepIdVarValueMapProducer_cfi")

# Load the cut-based electron ID
from PhysicsTools.SelectorUtils.tools.vid_id_tools import *
dataFormat = DataFormat.MiniAOD
switchOnVIDElectronIdProducer(process, dataFormat)

# Define which IDs to run  
my_id_modules = [
    'RecoEgamma.ElectronIdentification.Identification.cutBasedElectronID_RunIII_V1_cff'
]

# Add them to the VID producer
for idmod in my_id_modules:
    setupAllVIDIdsInModule(process,idmod,setupVIDElectronSelection)
Usage in Analysis¶
Accessing ID Results¶
# In your analyzer
edm::Handle<edm::ValueMap<bool>> veto_id_decisions;
edm::Handle<edm::ValueMap<bool>> loose_id_decisions;
edm::Handle<edm::ValueMap<bool>> medium_id_decisions;
edm::Handle<edm::ValueMap<bool>> tight_id_decisions;

event.getByToken(eleVetoIdMapToken_, veto_id_decisions);
event.getByToken(eleLooseIdMapToken_, loose_id_decisions);
event.getByToken(eleMediumIdMapToken_, medium_id_decisions);
event.getByToken(eleTightIdMapToken_, tight_id_decisions);

// For each electron
const auto el = electrons->ptrAt(i);
bool isVeto = (*veto_id_decisions)[el];
bool isLoose = (*loose_id_decisions)[el];
bool isMedium = (*medium_id_decisions)[el];
bool isTight = (*tight_id_decisions)[el];

